00:01:19,135 --> 00:01:19,440
that,

35
00:01:20,178 --> 00:01:22,650
you need to create a cloud environment

36
00:01:23,308 --> 00:01:25,267
and I'll keep the name default here.

37
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:29,521
Choose the trusted setup here regarding

38
00:01:29,585 --> 00:01:30,436
network access.

39
00:01:31,351 --> 00:01:33,326
If you give it full internet access, you of

40
00:01:33,358 --> 00:01:35,814
course have maximum flexibility and you

41
00:01:35,830 --> 00:01:38,078
might need that if your app, for example,

42
00:01:38,560 --> 00:01:41,658
needs to send API requests and you want all

43
00:01:41,771 --> 00:01:44,773
tests to run on that cloud environment. But

44
00:01:44,773 --> 00:01:47,053
of course with full internet access, you

45
00:01:47,069 --> 00:01:50,055
also have all the full internet threat, so

46
00:01:50,055 --> 00:01:51,837
to say. So I'll use the trusted one here.

47
00:01:52,062 --> 00:01:53,568
And now with that setup,

48
00:01:54,128 --> 00:01:56,996
you can either use Claude Code in the cloud

49
00:01:57,012 --> 00:01:59,352
from this web interface or also from your

50
00:01:59,416 --> 00:02:01,210
local client. I'll get back to that in a

51
00:02:01,210 --> 00:02:01,579
second.

52
00:02:02,139 --> 00:02:04,447
Here I'll first choose my repository. I got

53
00:02:04,543 --> 00:02:07,283
one branch there which I pushed to it yet at

