push to your main branch, you probably

102
00:04:02,489 --> 00:04:04,509
wouldn't want that. Instead, it creates a

103
00:04:04,509 --> 00:04:07,540
new branch and opens a pull request so that

104
00:04:07,540 --> 00:04:09,914
you can then review and merge those changes.

105
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:11,918
Now whilst it's working, it's also worth

106
00:04:11,966 --> 00:04:12,303
noting

107
00:04:13,057 --> 00:04:14,405
that you can also combine

108
00:04:14,982 --> 00:04:17,052
